# Turbo Best Practices

This document outlines best practices for using Turborepo in our monorepo, focusing on workspace configuration, task dependencies, and performance optimization.

## Workspace Configuration

- Organize packages by type (apps, packages, config, etc.)
- Use consistent package naming conventions
- Implement proper workspace dependencies in package.json
- Leverage package.json workspaces field correctly
- Keep turbo.json clean and well-structured
- Set appropriate access levels for packages

## Task Configuration

- Define reusable task pipelines in turbo.json
- Use explicit dependencies between tasks
- Implement proper caching strategies for each task
- Configure input/output files correctly for optimal caching
- Leverage env vars in pipeline definitions when needed
- Use task inheritance for common configurations

## Cache Optimization

- Configure proper outputs for each task for accurate caching
- Use .turbo/cache to store cache results
- Implement remote caching for CI/CD pipelines when appropriate
- Add proper gitignore patterns for cache directories
- Use cache priming for faster CI builds
- Configure appropriate cache invalidation

## Dependencies Management

- Use strict workspace protocols (workspace:*)
- Implement consistent versioning strategies
- Leverage npm/yarn/pnpm workspace features
- Avoid duplicated dependencies across packages
- Use peer dependencies appropriately
- Configure proper build order with dependencies

## CI/CD Integration

- Use turbo to parallelize CI workflows
- Implement proper caching in CI pipelines
- Configure concurrency settings for optimal performance
- Use proper pruning for deployment packages
- Leverage turbo for incremental builds

## Development Workflows

- Use filtered runs for faster development (--filter)
- Implement consistent dev scripts across packages
- Leverage Watch mode for development
- Use scoped commands for targeted operations
- Configure proper development dependencies
